---
description: InfoGenie development workflow and quality gates
alwaysApply: true
---

- Work autonomously from implementation to a merge-ready PR.
- Inspect relevant code, project instructions and tests before coding.
- Establish acceptance criteria covering user behavior, failure states,
  tenant/client isolation, permissions, missing data, verified zero,
  stale responses and affected UI/API/portal/export paths.
- Resolve routine implementation choices independently.
- Use one coding agent, followed by one focused read-only Security/QA
  review if available. Otherwise review directly and disclose it.
- Reuse existing patterns. Avoid unrelated refactors and dependencies.
- Keep each PR within 1,500 additions plus deletions.
- Run affected tests during development and required broader gates
  when implementation is ready.
- After corrections, rerun affected checks. Ensure required hosted CI
  passes on the final SHA; required integration/browser tests must
  execute with zero skips.
- Collect confirmed blockers in one review pass and fix them together.
  Record optional improvements separately.
- Inspect actual CI failure logs. Retry unchanged code only when
  evidence indicates a transient failure.
- Never disable checks or weaken assertions to obtain green CI.
- Continue through implementation, corrections, review and CI without
  requiring the user to relay instructions between stages.
- Stop only for genuine access blockers, material scope decisions or
  final human approval.
- Return PR URL, final SHA, diff size, verification, blockers and deferrals.
- Never merge or deploy without explicit user authorization.
- Preserve existing project rules and flag conflicts.
